[pytorch][WaitCounter] Add WITH_WAIT_COUNTER Macro and add unit tests (#172507)

Summary:
Add a new macro WITH_WAIT_COUNTER which allows us to run expressions within a wait counter easily. Usage:

```
int value = 0;
WITH_WAIT_COUNTER(execute_with_test, value = 42);
EXPECT_EQ(value, 42);
```
or
```
int value = 0;
value = WITH_WAIT_COUNTER(execute_with_test, [](){ return 42; });
EXPECT_EQ(value, 42);
```

Also, add some unit tests since this library doesn't have any.

