[Inductor][CPP] Improve mkldnn convolution layout propagation in Inductor (#169260)

Fixes #119183 #119181
During inductor lowering, when the `opcount` or number of reads exceed the thresholds, inductor will realize the current IR node with channels first memory layout. This may breaks the memory layout propagation when channels last optimization enabled on Inductor CPP backend (although there are processes to determine the loop order, such process is based on the index expression and has difficulty handling indirect indexes.), resulting in performance degradation.
A simple example:
```
import torch
import torch.nn as nn
import torch._inductor.config as config
config.freezing = True

class UpsampleModel(nn.Module):
    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__()
        self.conv = nn.Conv2d(64, 64, kernel_size=3, padding=1)
        self.upsample = nn.Upsample(scale_factor=2, mode="bilinear", align_corners=True)
        self.conv2 = nn.Conv2d(64, 16, kernel_size=3, padding=1)

    def forward(self, x):
        x = self.conv(x)
        x = self.upsample(x)
        x = self.conv2(x)
        x = torch.relu(x)
        return x

with torch.no_grad():
    model = UpsampleModel()
    model = torch.compile(model)

    x = torch.randn(32, 64, 64, 64)
    out = model(x)
