[Inductor][CPP] Fix check_bounds for inductor cpp backend (#180212)

Fixes https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/178244.

The node `check_bounds` is prefer to put index expression bound checks in `loads` so it runs before the memory access on CPP backend.
However, if the index expression may have already been CSE'd into `compute` by a prior `ops.index_expr` call, placing a reference to it in loads would be a forward reference, for example:
```
...
TORCH_CHECK((at::vec::VecMask<int64_t,2>::set(at::vec::VecMask<int64_t,2>::from(1), (at::vec::VecMask<int64_t,2>(tmp2 < at::vec::VectorizedN<int64_t,2>(ks1))), static_cast<int64_t>(9L))).all_masked(), "index out of bounds: tmp2 < ks1");
auto tmp8 = at::vec::VecMask<float,1>::from(in_ptr3 + static_cast<int64_t>(x0), static_cast<int64_t>(9L));
auto tmp0 = x0;
auto tmp1 = c10::convert<int64_t>(tmp0);
auto tmp2 = at::vec::VectorizedN<int64_t,2>::arange(tmp1, 1);
...
```
In that case, tmp2 is referenced but not defined yet, and we need to put bound checks to `compute`:
```
...
auto tmp8 = at::vec::VecMask<float,1>::from(in_ptr3 + static_cast<int64_t>(x0), static_cast<int64_t>(9L));
auto tmp0 = x0;
auto tmp1 = c10::convert<int64_t>(tmp0);
auto tmp2 = at::vec::VectorizedN<int64_t,2>::arange(tmp1, 1);
auto tmp3 = ks0;
auto tmp4 = c10::convert<int64_t>(tmp3);
auto tmp5 = at::vec::VectorizedN<int64_t,2>(tmp4);
auto tmp6 = at::vec::VecMask<int64_t,2>(tmp2 <= tmp5);
TORCH_CHECK((at::vec::VecMask<int64_t,2>::set(at::vec::VecMask<int64_t,2>::from(1), (at::vec::VecMask<int64_t,2>(tmp2 < at::vec::VectorizedN<int64_t,2>(ks1))), static_cast<int64_t>(9L))).all_masked(), "index out of bounds: tmp2 < ks1");
...
```

