Fix reflection_pad2d and replication_pad2d meta to preserve channels_last format (#179366)

The C++ CPU implementation in [`aten/src/ATen/native/ReflectionPad.cpp`](https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/main/aten/src/ATen/native/ReflectionPad.cpp#L258-L264) preserves the input's memory format when resizing the output for 4D tensors:

```cpp
if (ndim == 3) {
  output.resize_({nplane, output_h, output_w});
} else {
  if (input.is_quantized()) {
    output.resize_({nbatch, nplane, output_h, output_w});
  } else {
    output.resize_({nbatch, nplane, output_h, output_w},
        input.suggest_memory_format());
  }
}
```

This means that a channels_last input produces a channels_last output. The Python meta kernel was not passing the memory format:

```python
# Before (wrong) - always contiguous output
return input.new_empty((nbatch, nplane, output_h, output_w))

# After (correct) - preserves channels_last format
output = input.new_empty((nbatch, nplane, output_h, output_w))
if input.is_contiguous(memory_format=torch.channels_last):
    output = output.to(memory_format=torch.channels_last)
return output
```
