Fix mkldnn_rnn_layer_backward meta dtype and GRU bias shape (#179367)

The C++ implementation in [`aten/src/ATen/native/mkldnn/RNN.cpp`](https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/main/aten/src/ATen/native/mkldnn/RNN.cpp#L371-L383) has two behaviors the Python meta kernel was not matching:

**1. All gradient tensors are created as float32** regardless of input dtype:

```cpp
// Create diff_* ATen tensor and corresponding ideep tensor as fp32
auto diff_x_ =
    at::empty(input.sizes(), input.options().dtype(at::ScalarType::Float));
auto diff_hx_ =
    at::empty(hx_.sizes(), hx_.options().dtype(at::ScalarType::Float));
auto diff_cx_ =
    at::empty(cx_.sizes(), cx_.options().dtype(at::ScalarType::Float));
auto diff_w1_ = at::empty(
    weight_ih.sizes(), weight_ih.options().dtype(at::ScalarType::Float));
auto diff_w2_ = at::empty(
    weight_hh.sizes(), weight_hh.options().dtype(at::ScalarType::Float));
auto diff_b_ =
    at::empty(bias.sizes(), bias.options().dtype(at::ScalarType::Float));
```

**2. The bias gradient shape** comes from [`_shuffle_bias`](https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/main/aten/src/ATen/native/mkldnn/RNN.cpp#L207-L214), which for GRU concatenates two 3-gate biases into a 4-gate result:

```cpp
static Tensor _shuffle_bias(const Tensor& bias_ih, const Tensor& bias_hh, int64_t fn_mode) {
  if (static_cast<ideep::rnn_kind>(fn_mode) == ideep::rnn_kind::GRU) {
    std::vector<Tensor> b1 = bias_ih.chunk(3, 0);
    std::vector<Tensor> b2 = bias_hh.chunk(3, 0);
    return at::cat({b1[1]+b2[1], b1[0]+b2[0], b1[2], b2[2]}, 0);
  }
  return bias_ih + bias_hh;
}
```

The [`RNNParams`](https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/main/aten/src/ATen/native/mkldnn/RNN.cpp#L118-L128) struct confirms: GRU has `num_gates=3` but `num_bias_gates=4`:

```cpp
if (mode == ideep::rnn_kind::LSTM) {
  num_gates = 4;
  num_bias_gates = 4;
} else if (mode == ideep::rnn_kind::GRU) {
  num_gates = 3;
  num_bias_gates = 4;
} else {
  num_gates = 1;
  num_bias_gates = 1;
}
```

The Python meta was using wrong dtype and wrong bias shape:

```python
# Before (wrong) - inherits input dtype, uses weight2's shape for bias
diff_x = input.new_empty(input.shape)           # wrong dtype
diff_hx = hx_.new_empty(hx_.shape)              # wrong dtype
diff_b = weight2.new_empty(weight2.shape)        # wrong shape for GRU + wrong dtype

# After (correct) - forces float32, computes correct bias shape
diff_x = input.new_empty(input.shape, dtype=torch.float)
diff_hx = hx_.new_empty(hx_.shape, dtype=torch.float)
_GRU_MODE = 3
if mode == _GRU_MODE:
    bias_size = 4 * hidden_size
else:
    bias_size = weight2.shape[0]
diff_b = weight2.new_empty([bias_size], dtype=torch.float)
```
