[Symmetric Memory] Remove NCCL symmetric memory explicit dependency on process group (#183423)

## Summary

`NCCLSymmetricMemory` previously obtained its host-side `ncclComm_t` by
`dynamic_cast`-ing a process group's backend to `c10d::ProcessGroupNCCL*` and
calling `getCommPtr()`:
```cpp
auto* ncclPg = dynamic_cast<c10d::ProcessGroupNCCL*>(
    group->getBackend(c10::DeviceType::CUDA).get());
TORCH_CHECK(ncclPg != nullptr, "backend must be a NCCL process group");
comm_ = reinterpret_cast<ncclComm_t>(ncclPg->getCommPtr());
```
This hard-codes the assumption that the only thing that can drive NCCL
collectives in c10d is `ProcessGroupNCCL` itself. That makes it unyielding to extend for out of tree libs such as torchcomms.

### Implementation

This PR decouples `NCCLSymmetricMemory` from `ProcessGroupNCCL` by routing
host-comm lookup through the existing `NCCLDevCommManager` registry, keyed
by group name. Any backend that owns a NCCL comm publishes into
the registry; `NCCLSymmetricMemory` reads from it. The dynamic_cast and the
hard backend-type check go away.

## Downstream PR in Torchcomms

https://github.com/meta-pytorch/torchcomms/pull/2503

Enables pattern such as

```cpp
  // pytorch — NCCLSymmetricMemory (was: dynamic_cast<ProcessGroupNCCL*>)
  ncclComm_t comm = NCCLDevCommManager::get(device).get_comm(group_name);

  // pytorch — ProcessGroupNCCL now publishes into the registry at init
  NCCLDevCommManager::get(device).register_comm(group_uid, ncclComm);
  ncclComm_t comm = NCCLDevCommManager::get(device).get_comm(group_name);

  // pytorch — ProcessGroupNCCL now publishes into the registry at init
  NCCLDevCommManager::get(device).register_comm(group_uid, ncclComm);

  // Anyone who owns a ncclComm_t can register the same way — torchcomms
  // TorchCommNCCLX does this in registerWithSymmMem(group_name):
  NCCLDevCommManager::get(device).register_comm(group_name, nccl_comm_);

```

Use BackendWrapper shim to create PG backed by torchcomms

```python

  // So now symm_mem.rendezvous works over ANY backend that exposes a NCCL comm:
  ncclx_comm = torchcomms.new_comm("ncclx", cuda, name="...", store=store)   # owns a ncclComm_t under the hood
  pg = dist.ProcessGroup(...)                          # bare PG
  pg._register_backend(cuda, BackendType.NCCL, _BackendWrapper(ncclx_comm))
  pg._set_group_name("my_group")
  ncclx_comm.register_with_symm_mem("my_group")        # publishes into registry
  symm_mem.rendezvous(buf, group="my_group")           # finds comm via registry, no dynamic_cast
```
