Fix use-after-free in symbolic-shape runtime fusion guard (#183760)

The per-invocation guard lambda generated by `generateGuard` did:

    auto inputs = last(stack, N);
    drop(stack, N);
    for (size_t i = 0; i < N; ++i) {
      inputs[i].toTensor()...;
    }

`drop(stack, N)` destroys those last `N` IValues — refcount decrements on each contained Tensor — so the loop after it reads already-destroyed slots. ASAN catches the read as container-overflow inside `IValue::isTensor`. On non-ASAN builds the same access is a genuine use-after-free that survives only because the freed slab is not reused in the narrow window of the loop.

Copy the slice out of the stack before calling `drop()`, then use the local copy.

Reproduced under an ASAN build of pytorch on ROCm in around 17 tests in test/test_jit_fuser_te.py, including test_lstm, test_chunk_mul_one, test_dynamic_shapes, and test_channels_last_dims_dynamic.

